# Review Live-Streaming via Per-Agent JSON Output Implementation Plan

> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (if subagents available) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.

**Goal:** Make `entire review`'s Ctrl+O drill-in show in-progress agent output (tool calls, assistant messages) as the agents work, instead of dumping everything at end of run.

**Architecture:** The current parsers consume plain-text stdout from `claude -p` and `codex exec -`. Both CLIs only emit text to stdout when the model has finished generating, so the drill-in buffer stays at `[started]` for the whole run and the dashboard preview only populates at end. The fix is to switch each agent to its own JSONL streaming mode (`claude … --output-format stream-json --verbose` and `codex exec … --json`), which emits one JSON envelope per agent-side event (`assistant.message` for claude; `item.started`/`item.completed`/`turn.completed` for codex). The parsers become line-delimited JSON decoders, each dispatching by `type` and emitting our existing `Event` variants (`AssistantText`, `ToolCall`, `Tokens`, `Finished`). No PTY, no change to the AgentReviewer / Process / Sink interfaces.

**Tech Stack:** Go 1.26 · github.com/spf13/cobra · charm.land/bubbletea/v2 (TUI sink) · `encoding/json` · `bufio.Scanner` (NDJSON line splitter) · existing `cmd/entire/cli/agent/{claudecode,codex,geminicli}` packages · `cmd/entire/cli/review/types` template.

---

## Context

### Why the current plain-text parsers fail

`claude -p <prompt>` in default text mode and `codex exec --skip-git-repo-check -` both buffer their output until the model finishes generating. The empirical evidence (from the user's manual A/B test on 2026-05-12):

- `claude -p "say hi"` → 10s wall, output dumps at end.
- `codex exec -` → 20s wall, full chrome + response at end.
- During a real review the drill-in stays at `[started]` for both agents until the very last second, when N events arrive in a burst. This is the user-visible bug the brief described as "events arrive batched at end of run".

A previous attempt to fix this with PTY mode (route stdout through `pty.Open()` so isatty returns true) was reverted: the real agents change output shape under a TTY (cursor-rewriting / no newlines), so the parser saw zero `AssistantText` events. That history is in commits on `review-fix-progress-stream` worktree and should not be repeated.

### Why JSONL mode does fix it

Both CLIs emit ONE JSON envelope per logical agent event, with a newline between envelopes. When the agent issues a tool call we get `item.started` (codex) / `assistant tool_use` (claude) immediately, BEFORE the tool runs. When the agent emits a chunk of text we get one envelope per message. For a real review (lots of `Read`/`Bash`/`Grep` tool use, interleaved analysis text) this gives ~10-50 events per agent run, spread over the full duration.

### What the live JSON looks like

Captured manually on 2026-05-12 from the worktree shell. Stored as fixtures in the test directories.

**claude `--output-format stream-json --verbose`:**

```
{"type":"system","subtype":"hook_started", …}        ← multiple, ignore
{"type":"system","subtype":"hook_response", …}       ← multiple, ignore
{"type":"system","subtype":"init", …}                ← one, ignore
{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":"…"}], …}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"…assistant prose…"}], …}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"…","name":"Read","input":{…}}], …}}   ← only on tool-use turns
{"type":"user","message":{"content":[{"type":"tool_result", …}]}}                                       ← echoes, ignore
{"type":"rate_limit_event", …}                       ← ignore
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","duration_ms":…,"is_error":false,"result":"…","usage":{"input_tokens":…,"output_tokens":…,"cache_read_input_tokens":…,"cache_creation_input_tokens":…}}
```

**codex `exec --json`:**

```
{"type":"thread.started","thread_id":"…"}
{"type":"turn.started"}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"…","status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"…","aggregated_output":"…","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"…assistant text…"}}
{"type":"turn.completed","usage":{"input_tokens":…,"cached_input_tokens":…,"output_tokens":…,"reasoning_output_tokens":…}}
```

Codex's live JSON shape is **different** from the persisted-transcript shape in `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/transcript.go` — do not reuse that schema. The live shape is documented above; the parser must match it exactly.

### Anti-features (do not introduce)

- **No PTY.** Pipe-mode JSONL is sufficient. The previous PTY attempt broke the agents.
- **No backwards-compat for the old plain-text parser.** Once we switch argv, the old format is unreachable. Delete the old parser code paths, not behind a feature flag.
- **No new agent in this PR.** gemini-cli stays on its current parser; if streaming is wanted there it's a follow-up.
- **No throttling / coalescing of events in the TUI.** Per-event dispatch is intentional. PR #1184 already fixed the drill-in viewport for this.
- **Codex chrome filter (`output_filter.go`) is dead code under `--json`.** Remove it once tests no longer reference it. (Confirm with `grep -rn "FilterLine\|codex.Strip" cmd/` before deleting.)

