go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/... -count=1
go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/... -count=1
go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/... -count=1
mise run fmt && mise run lint
```

All should pass. The new tests should pass against the EXISTING parser code (they test behavior the parser already has — we're adding coverage, not changing behavior). If any new test fails, your test code is incorrect — re-read the parser's exit paths and align.

Commit as ONE commit (do NOT amend):

```bash
git add cmd/entire/cli/agent/
git commit -m "$(cat <<'EOF'
test(review): cover streaming, missing-terminal, and garbled-line paths

Address Tier A items from PR #1192 review:

- Add TestParseClaudeOutput_StreamsEventsBeforeEOF mirroring codex's
  io.Pipe + timeout-gated streaming guard. Also exercises the
  previously-uncovered tool_use content block path.
- Add TestParse{Claude,Codex}Output_NoTerminalEnvelopeMeansFailed for
  the truncated-stream → Finished{Success:false} branch.
- Add TestParse{Claude,Codex}Output_GarbledLineEmitsRunErrorAndContinues
  to lock the recover-and-continue contract for per-line JSON errors.
- Document codex's hard-coded Finished{Success:true} so a future
  schema addition that exposes turn-level errors gets wired through.
- Soften the "codex 0.130.0" version-pin comment to read as a contract.
- Replace the stale "no chrome filtering needed" comment in
  geminicli/reviewer.go with a description that doesn't reference
  deleted code.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
EOF
)"
```

## Report Format

When done, report:
- Status: DONE | DONE_WITH_CONCERNS | BLOCKED | NEEDS_CONTEXT
- Commit SHA
- Test results (which new tests pass)
- mise run lint result
- Anything unexpected

If any new test fails against the existing parser, that's a real bug and you should STOP and report it — do NOT modify the parser to make a test pass.

